From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:50:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Release each microtask's autorelease pool entries
 when it ends

With the QuickJS backend (js-quickjs), the shim keeps every value it
hands to Rust in an autorelease pool, which Servo drains between
tasks. A microtask checkpoint therefore kept every microtask it ran,
and everything the microtask referenced, alive until the task ended.
The checkpoint loop now opens a servo-quickjs AutoreleasePoolScope for
each microtask, JS jobs and Servo's own alike. The loop's roots are
written before they are read in each iteration, and what a microtask
leaves for later holds references of its own (Heap, Dom), which is
what the scope requires.

With release builds on ohos-main 4d542899ab6, whose Rust code is the
same as here: RSS grows by 3 MiB instead of 252 MiB over 10^6 awaits
in one task, and by 3 MiB instead of 69 MiB over a chain of 10^6
queueMicrotask calls; dom-bench's await loop takes 97 instead of
120 ms. 19 pages (7 runs each) are unchanged in time and memory.

The servo-quickjs pin in support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml moves from
879bfe9 to 78daccd ("mozjs: pool scopes for microtasks"), which adds
the scope and drains the pool entries of the incumbent-global trap
after each then()/await. The other four commits in between add pool
statistics (only in builds with QJS_POOL_STATS=1), drain the pool
through a raw pointer, fix two fuzz targets, and add tests. The
raw-pointer drain avoids a miscompile that released pooled objects
twice in optimized builds, but the shim still holds a &mut Cx across
calls that re-enter it, which Rust's aliasing rules forbid; a
servo-quickjs follow-up fixes that, the scope's drain included.

One subtest of jsurl-form-submit.tentative.html, a race between a
javascript: URL's result and the form submission it starts, passes
with this under parallel load and fails alone, as with SpiderMonkey;
it is marked [FAIL, PASS] for QuickJS.

Fork note: QuickJS only (feature js-quickjs); not for upstream.

Validation: WPT subset of 21 directories (7670 tests) with --js-engine quickjs and QJS_VERIFY_TRACING=1 (shim f4037c8; 78daccd only adds documentation, debug assertions and pool-statistics fixes): no verifier report; all unexpected results but three tests and three subtests also occur with the old pin 879bfe9, and of those six only the jsurl-form-submit subtest reproduced in 5 reruns; ./mach fmt and ./mach test-tidy.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written, tested and measured by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 components/script/runtime/job_queue.rs                       | 5 +++++
 support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml                            | 2 +-
 .../form-submission-0/jsurl-form-submit.tentative.html.ini   | 4 +++-
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/script/runtime/job_queue.rs b/components/script/runtime/job_queue.rs
index 6791a953180..a38a55909b5 100644
--- a/components/script/runtime/job_queue.rs
+++ b/components/script/runtime/job_queue.rs
@@ -232,6 +232,11 @@ pub(crate) fn job_queue_microtask_checkpoint(
     // and https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/7ae92e67d094086cd3e09918ec94b6278a948535/xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.cpp#1176
     // and its helper functions
     while unsafe { HasAnyMicroTasks(cx) } {
+        // QuickJS: release what this microtask kept alive in the autorelease pool, instead of at
+        // the end of the task. The roots above are written before they are read in each iteration,
+        // and what a microtask leaves for later holds references of its own.
+        #[cfg(feature = "js-quickjs")]
+        let _pool_scope = unsafe { js::quickjs::AutoreleasePoolScope::new() };
         unsafe { JS_DequeueNextMicroTask(cx, generic_task.handle_mut()) };
 
         // Notify the JS engine if the queue is now empty, enabling optimizations
diff --git a/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml b/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
index 45b4de1fd31..b62d51e5349 100644
--- a/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
+++ b/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
@@ -5,4 +5,4 @@
 # were tested with. The shim's version must match the mozjs version that Cargo.toml requires, or
 # Cargo leaves the patch unused.
 [patch.crates-io]
-mozjs = { git = "https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs", rev = "879bfe90ee0855fe9a63b7faba8c414ecdf7a37f" }
+mozjs = { git = "https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs", rev = "78daccddca57c745b830b5486b0e6bec4de40587" }
diff --git a/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/forms/form-submission-0/jsurl-form-submit.tentative.html.ini b/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/forms/form-submission-0/jsurl-form-submit.tentative.html.ini
index 640bea3a8dd..ea8ff616877 100644
--- a/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/forms/form-submission-0/jsurl-form-submit.tentative.html.ini
+++ b/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/forms/form-submission-0/jsurl-form-submit.tentative.html.ini
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
 [jsurl-form-submit.tentative.html]
   [Verifies that form submissions scheduled inside javascript: urls take precedence over the javascript: url's return value.]
-    expected: FAIL
+    expected:
+      if js_engine == "quickjs": [FAIL, PASS]
+      FAIL
